  ^{:line 84} [^{:val 22 :doc "R_USETYPE resolves to an *rtype, but no relocation is created. The\nlinker uses this as a signal that the pointed-to type information\nshould be linked into the final binary, even if there are no other\ndirect references. (This is used for types reachable by reflection.)\n"} R_USETYPE]





  ^{:line 90} [^{:val 23 :doc "R_USEIFACE marks a type is converted to an interface in the function this\nrelocation is applied to. The target is a type descriptor or an itab\n(in the latter case it refers to the concrete type contained in the itab).\nThis is a marker relocation (0-sized), for the linker's reachabililty\nanalysis.\n"} R_USEIFACE]





  ^{:line 96} [^{:val 24 :doc "R_USEIFACEMETHOD marks an interface method that is used in the function\nthis relocation is applied to. The target is an interface type descriptor.\nThe addend is the offset of the method in the type descriptor.\nThis is a marker relocation (0-sized), for the linker's reachabililty\nanalysis.\n"} R_USEIFACEMETHOD]



  ^{:line 100} [^{:val 25 :doc "R_USENAMEDMETHOD marks that methods with a specific name must not be eliminated.\nThe target is a symbol containing the name of a method called via a generic\ninterface or looked up via MethodByName(\"F\").\n"} R_USENAMEDMETHOD]





