  ^{:line 189} [^{:val 46 :doc "R_POWER_TLS_LE is used to implement the \"local exec\" model for tls\naccess. It resolves to the offset of the thread-local symbol from the\nthread pointer (R13) and is split against a pair of instructions to\nsupport a 32 bit displacement.\n"} R_POWER_TLS_LE]






  ^{:line 196} [^{:val 47 :doc "R_POWER_TLS_IE is used to implement the \"initial exec\" model for tls access. It\nrelocates a D-form, DS-form instruction sequence like R_ADDRPOWER_DS. It\ninserts to the offset of GOT slot for the thread-local symbol from the TOC (the\nGOT slot is filled by the dynamic linker with the offset of the thread-local\nsymbol from the thread pointer (R13)).\n"} R_POWER_TLS_IE]







  ^{:line 204} [^{:val 48 :doc "R_POWER_TLS marks an X-form instruction such as \"ADD R3,R13,R4\" as completing\na sequence of GOT-relative relocations to compute a TLS address. This can be\nused by the system linker to rewrite the GOT-relative TLS relocation into a\nsimpler thread-pointer relative relocation. See table 3.26 and 3.28 in the\nppc64 elfv2 1.4 ABI on this transformation.  Likewise, the second argument\n(usually called RB in X-form instructions) is assumed to be R13.\n"} R_POWER_TLS]




  ^{:line 209} [^{:val 49 :doc "R_POWER_TLS_IE_PCREL34 is similar to R_POWER_TLS_IE, but marks a single MOVD\nwhich has been assembled as a single prefixed load doubleword without using the\nTOC.\n"} R_POWER_TLS_IE_PCREL34]



  ^{:line 213} [^{:val 50 :doc "R_POWER_TLS_LE_TPREL34 is similar to R_POWER_TLS_LE, but computes an offset from\nthe thread pointer in one prefixed instruction.\n"} R_POWER_TLS_LE_TPREL34]






  ^{:line 220} [^{:val 51 :doc "R_ADDRPOWER_DS is similar to R_ADDRPOWER above, but assumes the second\ninstruction is a \"DS-form\" instruction, which has an immediate field occupying\nbits [15:2] of the instruction word. Bits [15:2] of the address of the\nrelocated symbol are inserted into this field; it is an error if the last two\nbits of the address are not 0.\n"} R_ADDRPOWER_DS]



  ^{:line 224} [^{:val 52 :doc "R_ADDRPOWER_GOT relocates a D-form + DS-form instruction sequence by inserting\na relative displacement of referenced symbol's GOT entry to the TOC pointer.\n"} R_ADDRPOWER_GOT]



  ^{:line 228} [^{:val 53 :doc "R_ADDRPOWER_GOT_PCREL34 is identical to R_ADDRPOWER_GOT, but uses a PC relative\nsequence to generate a GOT symbol addresses.\n"} R_ADDRPOWER_GOT_PCREL34]




  ^{:line 233} [^{:val 54 :doc "R_ADDRPOWER_PCREL relocates two D-form instructions like R_ADDRPOWER, but\ninserts the displacement from the place being relocated to the address of the\nrelocated symbol instead of just its address.\n"} R_ADDRPOWER_PCREL]




  ^{:line 238} [^{:val 55 :doc "R_ADDRPOWER_TOCREL relocates two D-form instructions like R_ADDRPOWER, but\ninserts the offset from the TOC to the address of the relocated symbol\nrather than the symbol's address.\n"} R_ADDRPOWER_TOCREL]




  ^{:line 243} [^{:val 56 :doc "R_ADDRPOWER_TOCREL_DS relocates a D-form, DS-form instruction sequence like\nR_ADDRPOWER_DS but inserts the offset from the TOC to the address of the\nrelocated symbol rather than the symbol's address.\n"} R_ADDRPOWER_TOCREL_DS]




  ^{:line 248} [^{:val 57 :doc "R_ADDRPOWER_D34 relocates a single prefixed D-form load/store operation.  All\nprefixed forms are D form. The high 18 bits are stored in the prefix,\nand the low 16 are stored in the suffix. The address is absolute.\n"} R_ADDRPOWER_D34]




  ^{:line 253} [^{:val 58 :doc "R_ADDRPOWER_PCREL34 relates a single prefixed D-form load/store/add operation.\nAll prefixed forms are D form. The resulting address is relative to the\nPC. It is a signed 34 bit offset.\n"} R_ADDRPOWER_PCREL34]

